    cover_note='Welcome to Session 6. Last time you saw how a language model predicts the next token, how it is trained by the Session 0 loop, and what sits inside a transformer block. Today we ask how a model like that becomes the assistant you use, what the main model families are, and how to judge claims about them. You see one task answered by two assistants, recorded, and you read a real model card.',
